-5Q8WpSg3rrwsoCMfWMHcCNRQX1eogeeKBO5H2CGoET6JCQkcuRMljZ1vCcbuo9I4K7N2wsXiTX5wqfQ4XPRetWIqekLox31-cf6Sqfjt1I-akFCzc77O2Pk64pTafKagpPEtX_WVrIJrIrWlt_4rkSIK2sjBFr95hMuhOgadQo1Y9jmDHpSm0hF5mjXuokQWPttCa9QMG1qL_IArdHdZnTNjv4-5Ol03clVKMR-3XHebYeOGw4SWV4sjiwO6PopLro2rX87RbTQC886eBFMnaIR4YAHrro91P2MEYItC1SE-pfC-y3mAXAt38pbJm8y28Kb3L7MPJ3v8WejcwhC9x2K98KSA6d3-0TJ03uSTY2zN02POfEFPbQ6UUkCpon6TLcCfmkpqW4UkYl2VS6SPe21MHMjqWsKceB-Ej9QXKphNmJIYA=","additionalProperties":{"reasoningItemId":"rs_066dcb40e59f6e13006adee6509d2c87d2ab8c50ef3e21ae71"}},{"$type":"text","text":"### 1. Who they are\n**Ned Fenn** has kept a crowded city inn running through enough hard seasons to stop expecting them to get easier.\n\n### 2. Where they stand\nNed knows [name of the fence]. The players want that name; Ned wants to keep the secret buried and will not give it up at the first ask.\n\n### 3. How they seem, and what is underneath\nThey listen with a weary tilt of the head, giving a tired, heartfelt attention even when they’d rather be left alone. Beneath the fatigue, Ned is guarding a secret they believe should stay buried. They also assume the adventurers all know one another.\n\n### 4. Levers\n- **Include Ned in what happens next** *(weakness: cannot bear being left out).* Their guarded look softens, though the ask costs them: “You’re going to do something with that name. Don’t shut me out—tell me where I fit, and I’ll tell you.”\n- **Show that you understand the secret is at risk, and offer to help keep it buried** *(characterWants: to keep a secret buried).* Ned studies you, head tilted. “If you’re asking because you mean to protect it, I’ll trust you with [name of the fence]. But don’t make me regret it.”\n\n### 5. Anti-levers\n- **Demand the name without addressing Ned’s wish to keep the secret buried** *(characterWants: to keep a secret buried).* Ned’s expression settles into weary refusal. “No. I’ve kept it quiet this long. I’m not handing it over just because you asked.”\n- **Treat Ned as an obstacle to push past** *(attitude: world-weary).* They let the silence stretch. “I’ve seen this sort of urgency before. It doesn’t make me trust you.”\n- **Ask about the tooth they lost** *(willNotDiscuss: how they lost a tooth).* Ned’s head turns away. “That isn’t what we’re talking about. Leave it alone.”\n\n### 6. Afterwards\n**Didn’t.** If the players leave without making Ned feel included or showing they’ll help keep the secret buried, Ned keeps [name of the fence] to themself."}],"messageId":"msg_066dcb40e59f6e13006adee65171c887d28240146aab9ede3e"}],"responseId":"resp_066dcb40e59f6e13006adee64b14dc87d2a8aa5b20b4862d23","conversationId":"resp_066dcb40e59f6e13006adee64b14dc87d2a8aa5b20b4862d23","modelId":"gpt-6-luna","createdAt":"2026-10-26T05:34:03+00:00","usage":{"inputTokenCount":1465,"outputTokenCount":1093,"totalTokenCount":2558,"cachedInputTokenCount":1056,"reasoningTokenCount":621}}}
